1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,430
Anyone who attacked American bombers from behind flew straight into their defensive fire.

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:06,800
So Egon Mayer attacked them head-on.

3
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:12,260
He was born in Konstanz in 1917 and joined the Luftwaffe in 1937.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:16,950
From December 1939 he flew with Fighter Wing 2 "Richthofen".

5
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:20,210
In the Battle of Britain he was shot down himself.

6
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:24,030
Once he swam in the English Channel for an hour before he was rescued.

7
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:30,010
From August 1942 American B-17s attacked targets in France by day.

8
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:34,860
They flew in tight formations and covered each other with heavy machine guns.

9
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:37,310
Only the nose of the bombers was lightly armed.

10
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:42,960
On 23 November 1942 Mayer attacked head-on over St Nazaire

11
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:47,240
and claimed two B-17s and a B-24 shot down.

12
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,660
With Georg-Peter Eder he turned this into a tactic:

13
00:00:50,690 --> 00:00:54,260
come in from the front, fire a short burst, then pull away steeply.

14
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:58,260
The head-on attack largely became the standard method of German fighters.

15
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:03,080
The Americans later added an extra gun turret under the nose of the B-17.

16
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:07,520
In July 1943 Mayer became commander of his wing.

17
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:13,430
In September 1943 he was credited with three B-17s within 19 minutes.

18
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:20,020
In February 1944 he became the first fighter pilot on the Channel front to reach 100 victories.

19
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:25,090
On 2 March 1944 he led an attack on B-17s near Sedan.

20
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:30,350
American P-47 escort fighters shot down his Focke-Wulf.

21
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:32,250
It crashed near Montmédy.

22
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,760
Egon Mayer was 26 years old.

23
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:38,800
He was credited with 102 aerial victories, all in the West.
